	(text "\"Fault Simulation Connector\", which simulates \na situation in which the Sensor is generating\na VDIAG error (voltage under 0.39 V)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 274.828 173.482 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "03fdfeed-45ed-4110-8c91-e27b017b75c7")
	)
	(text "Differential Amplifier"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 263.906 16.256 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.286 2.286)
				(thickness 0.4572)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "062ff07b-008f-4ccf-bde8-e34f952e8d47")
	)
	(text "This Voltage Divider defines the Threshold under which\nthe VDIAG signal coming from the Sensor is interpreted\nas an error. VDIAG has two different operating states:\n	- NO ERROR:	VDIAG Voltage is always > 0.5V\n	- ERROR:	VDIAG Voltage is always < 0.39V\nIn practice, whatever threshold in the range [0.39V; 0.5V]\nis acceptable to recognise VDIAG errors. Because of this\nrange can not be achieved with both 5% Toll. resistors, \nand so one of them must be 1% (10.5k).\nThe \"Worst Case\" voltage values generated by the\nVoltage Divider are:\n\r\n	V_max 	= 3.366V * (10.605k / (10.605k + 64.6)) =\n			= 0.4747 V \n\n	V_min 	= 3.234V * (10.395k / (10.395k + 71.4k)) = \n			= 0.4110 V "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 210.82 208.788 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "0ac19a07-933c-4767-b624-d833fabdb63f")
	)
	(text "To be mounted ONLY \nin the case a 2nd order \nfilter is needed\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 64.77 76.708 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "0c6fd155-cd51-4a3b-bb77-95ca53d2482e")
	)
	(text "To be mounted ONLY \nin the case a 2nd order \nfilter is needed\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 64.77 155.448 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "1f59fbd4-a45c-431b-b651-1a6a32c0e744")
	)
	(text "Anti-Aliasing Filter\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 73.66 16.51 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.286 2.286)
				(thickness 0.4572)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "27fd7bb1-f8b1-4db5-b091-c4fbdccdfe06")
	)
	(text "Comparator outputs use Pull-Up to 3v3 digital, \nbecause because their signal is an input for \nthe FPGA digital domain, while the comparison \nitself needs to be in the Analog domain \n(because Vdiag is referenced to Analog 3v3)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 302.768 196.85 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "339019f9-f892-40b5-b589-39d99259b358")
	)
	(text "This Voltage Divider must simulate the VDIAG signal \nwhen error is present (Voltage < 0.39V). Because \nprecision is not needed, 5% Toll. resistances are\nused, and the values are chosen guaranteeing the \ngenerated voltage is ALWAYS < 0.39V:\n\n	V_max 	= 3.3V * (10.5k / (10.5k + 95k)) = \n			= 0.335 V "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 210.82 180.594 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "38b6330f-2f32-404a-a642-607fac6d5067")
	)
	(text "To be mounted ONLY \nin the case a 2nd order \nfilter is needed\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 64.77 36.068 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "4041924b-d0d4-4541-b402-9e5a9c5f2135")
	)
	(text "\"Fault Simulation Connector\", which just \ndisconnects the ADC Serial DataOut pin to\nthe reader. \nHiZ and GND faults can be simulated with\nthis connector "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 378.968 46.99 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "562766da-7120-471b-83a7-dd401923ccf7")
	)
	(text "Sensor"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 287.528 167.894 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.286 2.286)
				(thickness 0.4572)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "5ee6d5f7-a359-4385-a114-704401f79af5")
	)
	(text "To be mounted ONLY \nin the case a 2nd order \nfilter is needed\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 64.77 116.078 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "606769a9-97bf-4016-97b7-f7d5e72ea02a")
	)
	(text "\"Fault Simulation Connector\", which disconnects power \nsupply for one of the two sensing channels.\nOnly the Stuck-Open fault can be simulated by this\nconnector"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 81.788 202.692 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "62ac0efd-ba20-4d4b-b1bd-16c6d1cfab2d")
	)
	(text "From LED datasheet the Typical Voltage drop at 5 mA is 2.95V.\nKnowing this, I can compute the series resistor:\n	R = (3.3V - V_forw_LED) / 5 mA = 70 Ohm\n	--> E12 series (5% Toll.), R = 82 Ohm\n\nIf the Actual Forward Voltage of the LED is higher, it will simply light up with\nlower luminosity, so using the typical Forward Voltage value is ok (I don't need to \nbe precise on the actual current flowing in the LED, I just need it to light up)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 54.102 243.078 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "641dffa7-1db6-4dc3-8bf8-43a3153e5eba")
	)
	(text "The \"Sensor Board\" recives 5V Supply from its Master board, the \"Human Side Board\".\nThose 3.8V are DC/DC generated, and are fed through a cable harness, so they must \nconsidered noisy and not suitable for reference-sensitive Analog circuit. \n\nThis Power Supply circuit is developed using the WEBENCH TI Online Tool,\nallowing to define the LDO circuit that fits the design requirements. \nMore details in that report"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 19.05 204.47 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "7ef1610b-04bd-4a54-8b1e-af9aae2c80b5")
	)
	(text "1st Order Filter"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 40.64 118.11 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "83ca1f20-7fdd-4b8b-82c1-d4611bd76385")
	)
	(text "\"Fault Simulation Connector\", which just disconnects\none of the Sensor outputs. Stuck-Open and \nStuck-to-GND faults can be simulated by this \nconnector"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 95.25 49.53 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "89283601-4578-4c65-849b-802afe0df4ed")
	)
	(text "ADC"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 364.744 16.256 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.286 2.286)
				(thickness 0.4572)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "8b1a25a1-88fe-4f9d-8c2c-2ed8421e13eb")
	)
	(text "Connectors"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 355.6 226.568 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.286 2.286)
				(thickness 0.4572)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "8dd12e61-4cf4-4fe0-b37d-5b0acd8f6fb4")
	)
	(text "1st Order Filter"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 40.64 157.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "91571858-2c6d-4ee3-8bb8-968f834b436e")
	)
	(text "(1 filter for each differential output channel of Sensor)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 74.422 20.066 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
			)
		)
		(uuid "919d2f14-0a0e-49b3-93ed-df5a2b8368e1")
	)
	(text "1st Order Filter"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 40.64 78.74 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "9d011dad-69ee-4c9a-821a-4c80d910fad2")
	)
	(text "Power Supply"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 70.866 195.58 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.286 2.286)
				(thickness 0.4572)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "aa2dcd1d-dde0-4c3b-a0f3-1e5e6b512492")
	)
	(text "Pull-Up resistors are used in the ADCs CS inputs. The idea is that the default state of this control\npin (CS) in ensured even during FPGA's configuration phase (at startup time or after reset).\nCS = HIGH ensures that no ADC conversion is started\n\r\nPull-down resistors are used on the MUX selection inputs. The idea is to ensure a defined logic \nlevel even when the FPGA outputs are not yet configured (during startup or after reset), avoiding\npossible fast switching and undefined behaviors.\nSEL = LOW selects the S1 input, preventing the MUX from switching unpredictably due to \na floating control signal.\r\n\r\nThe resistor value is very high because this should not consume\nhigh static power:\n	P_loss = (3.3V)^2 / 100 kOhm = 0.11mW"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 238.506 238.76 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "aa77edb7-ea49-4d3b-a475-8dd7ff2d529b")
	)
	(text "ADC MUX"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 173.736 16.51 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.286 2.286)
				(thickness 0.4572)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "b39fad67-0c50-44ce-8985-674ac94eda89")
	)
	(text "FPGA Dev. Board"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 171.958 205.994 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.286 2.286)
				(thickness 0.4572)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "b458eefe-2011-4703-b6a1-265596cb1908")
	)
	(text "Common Mode filter. \nCommon Mode filter Cap. should be at least 10 times smaller than \nthe Differential Cap. to avoid transforming the Common Mode\nsignal into Differential Signal (basically inducing error in \nthe real measurement) due to the Common Mode Cap. mismatch \n(due to tollerances)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 34.798 65.024 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "b64d63f0-647f-4ec9-ad9f-9feabba4d8dd")
	)
	(text "1st Order Filter"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 40.64 38.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "c14c6372-1144-4d00-8fb5-6ada988149ca")
	)
	(text "Power Supply Interface"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 332.994 231.14 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.4572)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "c729ea5a-322e-434d-83b3-2a99458c9d5e")
	)
	(text "Sensor SPI Interface"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 379.984 231.394 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.4572)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "d74eb9db-2607-4e09-85cb-ee096ccde11e")
	)
	(text "Termination resistance for the MISO line. To be mounted as close as \npossible to the line driver (in theory near FPGA pin, but because of \ndevelopment board usage, place this resistor as near as possible to FPGA \nconnector).\n\nTo be mounted only if ringing problem arise on SPI (it is also possible \nto reduce the SPI frequency to mitigate the problem on the data lines, \nbut not on the CLK lines)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 136.652 277.622 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "e8ddf58e-60c9-4c37-b3ce-23dc63c54586")
	)
	(text "The voltage divider uses fairly high resistance values in order to reduce the\nstatic power consumption of the circuit\n	I = 3.3V / (2 * 47 kOhm) = 35 uA\n	P = 35 uA * 3.3V = 0.115 mW\n\nThe Capacitor is used to filter out noise and ripple on the Supply Line. \nThis noise is likely already very small, because of the LDO usage, but this \nfilter ensures to not generate a dependency between the ADC input and \nVref, as expected in the error model used (Vref only influences the Reference \nVoltage of the ADC, but not the Input Voltage)\n\nThe Filter has the following Cutoff frequency (exact frequency is not important, \nbut it must have have a small enough cutoff in order to efficently filter \nhigh frequency noises that can come from other subsystems):\n	Req = 47kOhm / 2 = 23.5 kOhm\n	f_cutoff = 1 / (2*pi*Req*C) = 68 Hz"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 209.296 149.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "ed47a8bc-c4e5-4835-b9df-d9b9c5357993")
	)
	(text "INA is a Subtractor with integrated balanced resistors, producing a differential \ngain of 0.5 (because it is INA500 version B)\n\nIts output is then computed as: V_out = (0.5 * (V_IN+ - V_IN-)) + V_ref\n\nV_ref volatge, as specified in the INA daatsheet, in directly connected to the internal \nresistors, and so it should be provided with a very high input impedance to avoid any \ninfluence on the resistive network (which is very sensitive of mismatches, to obtain \na good CMRR) \n\nIn practice, the V_ref voltage is generated by a simple Voltage Divider, but is connected \nto the INA's Vref pin via a Voltage Follower, to guarantee a that the voltage is\nfed to Vref pin with a very small impedance. "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 209.55 129.794 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "fa9c306c-57dd-4b0e-85ef-4924e350d471")
	)
